s:** the JSON file stores a `next_id` counter alongside the notes, so ids are never reused after a delete.\n- **Misuse:** `argparse` handles it. Unknown commands, missing arguments and a non-numeric id for `delete` all exit with status 2 and a usage message on stderr.\n- **Other behaviour:** `list --tag` takes a single tag, since the spec only describes one filter. Saves write to a temporary file and then replace the real one, so a failed write can't leave a half-written `notes.json`.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- the empty list\n- adding with tags and listing them\n- the tag filter\n- case-insensitive search\n- delete, including that ids aren't reused\n- deleting an unknown id\n- misuse exit codes","ttft_ms":3231,"type":"result","duration_ms":27531,"uuid":"31a358f2-fffc-4698-b857-bc0d50a84412","ttft_stream_ms":1016,"time_to_request_ms":44,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":12,"system_prompt":9,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":6,"input_hooks":0,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":2,"engine_pickup":0,"autocompact":1,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":7,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":2,"request_build":2},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":0,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":66,"time_to_request_major_faults":69,"first_content_frame_ms":1016,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
